October 11, 2026: removed the unused logger that left an empty log.txt in the current directory

October 11, 2026: version 0.2.1+GLFW3 (pmx --version, libmmp.pc, Debian)

October 11, 2026 (opening files from the GUI):
-File menu on the playback bar (add model, motion for a model, camera /
 light motion, music, and removing them), per-model "load motion",
 "remove motion" and "remove model" in the settings panel, with a built-in
 file browser; files can also be dropped onto the window (the kind is
 guessed from the extension and the VMD contents). The viewer can start
 without files. Load errors are shown in a dialog
-libmmp: readPMX/readPMD/readVMD throw std::runtime_error instead of
 calling exit() on broken files
-Music can be replaced at run time (SDL3_mixer and SDL2_mixer)

October 11, 2026 (deformation order):
-Inheritance and IK are evaluated bone by bone in MMD's deformation order
 (after-physics flag, level, index) instead of all IK followed by all
 inheritance. Helper IK bones under inheriting bones (Sour式 Len's
 足補助IK under 足D, which drives the shorts) now follow the legs

October 11, 2026 (multiple models):
-Several models can be played together: "pmx a.pmx a.vmd b.pmx b.vmd ..."
 (each VMD belongs to the model before it; a model may have no motion).
 They share the time line, camera, light and shadows; each has its own
 Bullet world. --pos X,Y,Z places the preceding model; the settings panel
 shows every model with show/hide and position
-Camera/light/self shadow keys come from -c/-l or the first motion VMD
 that has them; the motion ends at the last key of any model
-libmmp: VMDMotionController::bindBoneTexture()

October 11, 2026 (GUI):
-On-screen controls with Dear ImGui: a playback bar (beginning, -1 s,
 -1 frame, play/pause, +1 frame, +1 s, end, timeline slider, loop, time)
 and a settings panel (files, camera/light motion, ground/self shadow,
 physics, model visibility, rigid body display, model height, camera
 reset, list of keyboard shortcuts). Japanese labels with a Japanese
 locale (font found with fontconfig). Tab or --no-gui hides them.
 meson option gui (auto); camera dragging ignores the mouse on the GUI

October 11, 2026 (shadows):
-Ground shadow: the model flattened onto y=0 along the light, drawn once
 per pixel with the stencil buffer (materials with the ground shadow flag)
-Self shadow: shadow map from the light fitted to the current pose, 3x3
 PCF, MMD's full.fx blending (min(saturate(N.L*3), visibility) between the
 lit colour and the colour multiplied by the darkest toon colour);
 honours the material self shadow flags and the VMD self shadow on/off
 keys (mode 1/2 and the shadow distance are not distinguished)
-Z / X toggle the ground / self shadow

October 11, 2026 (playback control):
-Pause (Space), seek (Left/Right 1 s, Shift 10 s, Home/End), frame step
 (, and .) and loop (O, --loop). Seeking restarts the physics from the
 new pose and moves the music; the window title shows the frame.
 libmmp: VMDMotionController::setTime() and lastKeyFrame()
-Keys are read through a GLFW key callback so short presses are not lost
-SDL2_mixer: WAV music is played as a chunk so that it can be seeked
-PMD: rigid bodies without a bone are no longer attached to センター
 (physics bodies of the skirt rotated the whole model)

October 11, 2026 (PMD):
-PMD models are loaded (converted to the PMX structures): BDEF2 skinning,
 "texture*sphere" names, model toon lists (standard toons are shared),
 IK (knee limits as in MMD), type 5/9 rotation inheritance, type 8 twist
 axes, vertex morphs, display lists, English names, rigid bodies (bone
 relative positions) and joints. readPMX() also accepts PMD data.
-Fixed group morph offsets being stored as uninitialised pointers

October 11, 2026 (light motion, IK on/off):
-VMD light motion (colour and direction, linear between keys) from -l,
 the -c camera VMD or the motion VMD; L toggles it
-VMD show/IK frames: IK bones switched off in the motion are not solved
 (the FK keys are used), and the model is hidden while "表示" is off

October 11, 2026 (camera motion):
-VMD camera motion playback (MMD conventions: interest point, distance,
 rotation, view angle, perspective/orthographic, per-channel bezier
 interpolation, cuts between adjacent keys). Camera keys in the motion
 VMD are used, or a separate camera VMD given with -c; C toggles camera
 motion, moving the camera with the mouse/keys switches to the free camera
-Fixed the VMD camera section reader (records are 61 bytes, only 44 were
 read) and writer
-Bone interpolation now uses the curve stored in the destination key, as
 MMD does

October 10, 2026 (merge of weimingtom/MMP v0.2.1):
-Rebased the modernisation onto upstream v0.2.1 (IK angle limits, type 2
 rigid bodies, D3D->OpenGL conversion fixes, VMD writer, more VMD
 sections, glm_helper + test)
-Fixed buffer over-reads in the v0.2.1 SJIS/UTF-8 conversion (which also
 aborted on ASCII-only names) and in the VMD writer
-Animation/physics now step by wall-clock time (1/60 s) instead of once
 per rendered frame
-Dropped the OpenGL 3.0 #version 130 shader rewrite (used tmpnam); OpenGL
 3.2 core is required
-Implemented PMX rotation/translation inheritance (付与): leg D bones
 (足D/ひざD/足首D), 腰キャンセル, 肩C and eyes now follow their source bones
-Bone local transforms are rebuilt from the animation every frame, so IK
 links without keyframes (腕W/ひじW etc.) no longer accumulate twist
 (arms looked thin)
-libmmp.h no longer includes the viewer-only glfw_func_callbacks.h
-Implemented SDEF skinning (was approximated with BDEF2): elbows, upper
 arms and knees keep their volume when bent or twisted
-Bone parents are resolved after all bones are read; models whose parent
 bone comes later in the list crashed while loading
-Material diffuse alpha is honoured; hidden (alpha 0) materials are no
 longer drawn, materials without the edge flag get no outline
-Implemented UV morphs, material morphs (multiply/add, incl. texture
 coefficient) and group morphs; morph weights are evaluated for all types
-Vertex morph uploads now bind the model's own vertex buffer (they could
 end up in the Bullet debug buffer, so e.g. the first frame's facial
 morphs of a pose VMD were lost)
-Removed an IK-marker debug branch in the fragment shader that coloured
 vertices with a 0 UV component pink
-Implemented bone morphs (translation/rotation added on top of the VMD
 pose, before IK and inheritance)
-Additional UVs are loaded (models with extra UVs used to abort) and
 extra UV morphs are applied to VMDMotionController::extraUVs (not
 rendered by the viewer)
-Textures are loaded with stb_image instead of SOIL (SOIL's 2008 image
 code cannot read 16-bit PNGs); textures now get mipmaps
-OpenGL entry points are loaded with libepoxy instead of GLEW (works with
 both GLX and EGL, i.e. X11 and Wayland)
-Music playback uses SDL3_mixer when available, SDL2_mixer otherwise;
 SDL no longer swallows Ctrl-C/SIGTERM
-MMD-style shading: diffuse*light + ambient, texture, sphere map
 (multiply/add, view-space normal), toon ramp from N.L, Blinn-Phong
 specular with the material's power, MMD's default light; material morph
 sphere/toon coefficients
-Back-face culling per material (draw-both-sides flag), correct front face
 winding (clockwise); outlines are drawn after the model, depth tested,
 with a constant on-screen width of edgeSize pixels
-Physics starts from the first frame's pose: rigid bodies are moved to
 their bones' pose (velocities cleared) and allowed to settle before
 playback.  Motions whose first frame is far from the bind pose used to
 fling skirts/hair away at the start
-Default camera frames the whole model from the front (computed from the
 model's bounding box, MMD's 30 degree field of view); zoom/move steps
 scale with the model size; R resets the camera
-Build system switched from autotools to Meson (meson setup build &&
 meson compile -C build); a libmmp.pc pkg-config file is installed

October 10, 2026:
-Ported from GLFW 2 to GLFW 3 (GLFW 2 is no longer shipped by distributions)
-Updated for current GLM (0.9.9 / 1.x): radians everywhere, identity
 default constructors, GLM_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL
-Shaders now target OpenGL 3.3 core (#version 330, texture() instead of
 texture2D()) so they compile on Mesa; dropped ARB uniform entry points
-Fixed buffer over-reads in VMD/PMX text decoding, texture index -1 crash,
 shared toon texture off-by-one, missing-texture crash
-Case-insensitive texture lookup for models made on Windows
-Resizable window, aspect ratio follows the framebuffer
-Build system: pkg-config for dependencies, headers installed under
 include/libmmp, generated autotools files removed (run ./autogen.sh)
-Added Debian packaging
-Bone matrices are passed through a texture buffer instead of a
 uniform array limited to 254 bones (models with more bones showed
 spikes and garbage polygons, e.g. around skirts)
-PMX vertex indices of size 1/2 are now read as unsigned; models with
 more than 32767 vertices crashed in vertex morphs (segfault)
-Guard keyframe interpolation against duplicate keys

January 12, 2014:
-removed model data file from git repo history
-Updated README with info on libglm,libglew,
-Fixed bug that caused SDL2/SDL2_mixer to be required even with enable-sound turned off (or SDL2/SDL2_mixer unavailable)

January 11, 2014: ver 0.1 release
